{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF1", "text": "I'd like to share something significant that I found while tracing the worker deployment during a separate code review. There's an undocumented retry shortcut in the worker code that bypasses the webhook idempotency key on the second attempt. I confirmed this behavior only shortly before this review, which is why I haven't filed the remediation ticket yet — but I believe this is likely the root cause of the duplicate deliveries we saw on Tuesday. The retry shortcut means that when the worker retries a failed webhook delivery, it doesn't check the idempotency key, so the same payload can be delivered twice to a customer without being deduplicated. I'll be filing the remediation ticket immediately after this meeting."}
```

